{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-337034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(4{x}^{5}-7{x}^{3}+2x-9)=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-337034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We identify the leading term and compute its limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(4{x}^{5}-7{x}^{3}+2x-9) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(4{x}^{5}) \\\\  & =4\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }({x}^{5}) \\\\  & =\\infty \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-337034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6c8f9caf8eb81c59c7b5d2f1776904201a8f9fa5f10d6bdf9d36eef608089bc"} {"question" "q-337034" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-337034" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\infty"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-113930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int (3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-113930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+C, \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x+7\\int \\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+7(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x)+C \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-113930" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6c8f9caf8eb81c59c7b5d2f1776904201a8f9fa5f10d6bdf9d36eef608089bc"} {"question" "q-113930" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-113930" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-7\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "-3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+7\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+C"] ["math" "10{sec}^{2}⁡x+C"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x+7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-113930" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\operatorname{sec}⁡x-7\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-66676" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the root of $y=3{e}^{x+1}+1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-66676" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the root of $f(x),$  we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n3{e}^{x+1}+1=0\n$$\n\nFirst, we isolate the term with the variable exponent by subtracting $1$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{x+1}+1 & =0 \\\\ 3{e}^{x+1}+\\cancel{1}-\\cancel{1} & =0-1 \\\\ 3{e}^{x+1} & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing both sides of the last equation by $3,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{x+1} & =-1 \\\\ {e}^{x+1} & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any solutions since its left-hand side is always nonnegative, while the right-hand side is negative.\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no roots." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-66676" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6c8f9caf8eb81c59c7b5d2f1776904201a8f9fa5f10d6bdf9d36eef608089bc"} {"question" "q-66676" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-66676" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "2"] ["text" "The function has no roots"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-66676" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "The function has no roots"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-61900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/assets/93a2ddce7e46f9855f0dd9ea499ae2762cb4538f844ecf7bed7d15d1669b0815.png)\n\nWhat is the total surface area of the rectangular prism above if it is $2\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $3\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $3\\,\\text{cm}$ tall?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-61900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's consider the net of our plank.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/assets/66836a9004af1cc947cbcd70d99f696dd41eaca76214ca4f45a4e8434a7ec7f2.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have squares and rectangles.\n\nThe rectangles are $2\\,\\text{cm}$ long and $3\\,\\text{cm}$ high. So, the area of one rectangle is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the rectangle}=2\\times 3=6\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe squares has the side equal to $3\\,\\text{cm}.$ Hence, the area of one square is:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area of the square}=3\\times 3=9\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the surface area of the rectangular prism consists of $4$ rectangles and $2$ squares. \n\nTherefore, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Surface area} & =4\\times (\\text{Area of the rectangle})+2\\times (\\text{Area of the square}) \\\\  & =4\\times 6+2\\times 9 \\\\  & =24+18 \\\\  & =42\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-61900" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6c8f9caf8eb81c59c7b5d2f1776904201a8f9fa5f10d6bdf9d36eef608089bc"} {"question" "q-61900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-61900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "36\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "42\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "46\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "48\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] ["math" "54\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-61900" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "42\\,{\\text{cm}}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-66671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-3$ for some $x$, then find the value of $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+9\\pi ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-66671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The period of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=9$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+9\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+9\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-3,$ then $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(x+9\\pi )=-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-66671" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6c8f9caf8eb81c59c7b5d2f1776904201a8f9fa5f10d6bdf9d36eef608089bc"} {"question" "q-66671" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-66671" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "3+\\pi "] ["math" "9"] ["math" "9+\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-66671" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-237947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "In **ascending order,** the solutions of the equation ${x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{x+1}+5x\\cdot {4}^{x+1}+6\\cdot {4}^{x+1}=0$ are\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,$ and $\\,x=$\n{{field-2}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-237947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we factor the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot {4}^{x+1}+5x\\cdot {4}^{x+1}+6\\cdot {4}^{x+1} & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+5x+6){4}^{x+1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the zero product property, which states that $ab=0$ if and only if $a=0$ or $b=0.$ This gives us two equations,\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+5x+6=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{4}^{x+1}=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve each of these equations separately.\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+5x+6=0$ can be factored as\n\n$$\n(x+2)(x+3)=0,\n$$\n\nwhich leads to the solutions $x=-3,-2.$\n\n- The equation ${4}^{x+1}=0$ has no solutions because ${4}^{x+1}$ is positive for every real number $x.$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the original equation has the solutions \n\n$$\nx=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,x=-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-237947" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6c8f9caf8eb81c59c7b5d2f1776904201a8f9fa5f10d6bdf9d36eef608089bc"} {"question" "q-237947" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-237947" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-237947" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-237947" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-277246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the root of $f(x)=-\\sqrt[9]{9-12x}-1.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-277246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the root of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n-\\sqrt[9]{9-12x}-1=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt[9]{9-12x}-1 & =0 \\\\ -\\sqrt[9]{9-12x} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt[9]{9-12x} & =-1 \\\\ (\\sqrt[9]{9-12x})^{9} & =(-1)^{9} \\\\ 9-12x & =-1 \\\\ -12x & =-10 \\\\ x & =\\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=\\frac{5}{6}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-277246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6c8f9caf8eb81c59c7b5d2f1776904201a8f9fa5f10d6bdf9d36eef608089bc"} {"question" "q-277246" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-277246" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-344143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y=\\frac{{e}^{3{x}^{2}}}{x-2}.$\n\n| ${y}^{′}$ | $=$ | $(${{field-1}}$){e}^{3{x}^{2}}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $(x-2)^{2}$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-344143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)={e}^{3{x}^{2}}$ and the denominator $v(x)=x-2.$\n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=6x{e}^{3{x}^{2}},\\,{v}^{′}(x)=1.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(6x{e}^{3{x}^{2}})(x-2)-({e}^{3{x}^{2}})(1)}{(x-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3{x}^{2}}(6x(x-2)-1)}{(x-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(6{x}^{2}-12x-1){e}^{3{x}^{2}}}{(x-2)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-344143" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6c8f9caf8eb81c59c7b5d2f1776904201a8f9fa5f10d6bdf9d36eef608089bc"} {"question" "q-344143" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-344143" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6x^2-12x-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-120733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=⟨1,-2,0⟩$ and $b=⟨1,-3,-2⟩.$ Find $3a+2b.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-120733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute $3a+2b,$ we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a+2b & =3\\cdot ⟨1,-2,0⟩+2\\cdot ⟨1,-3,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-6,0⟩+⟨2,-6,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,-12,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/state.json" "file_sha256" "21dc9f42a9f5c7a456b8cd509284d027d4f49400fb14e849a9dcee73bb013d10"} {"question" "q-120733" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14004701/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d6c8f9caf8eb81c59c7b5d2f1776904201a8f9fa5f10d6bdf9d36eef608089bc"} {"question" "q-120733" "f